<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i-1)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null ==> this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1))));</code>

However, the above assertion seems to have a logical error based on the intended specification. The correct assertion should ensure that the elements from the specified index to the old size of the list are shifted correctly. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i));</code>

This assertion states that for every valid index from the specified index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position in the new list is equal to the element at the current position in the old list.
