<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i-1)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

However, the provided comment seems to have a slight misinterpretation. The correct interpretation should be that for every valid index from the specified index to the old size of the list, the element at the current position should be equal to the old element at the previous position. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

But since the element at the `index` position is newly added, the correct assertion should account for the shift. Here is the accurate assertion:

<code>assert \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

This ensures that starting from the position right after the newly inserted element, each element is shifted correctly.
