<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null) => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

However, the above assert statement seems to incorrectly interpret the requirement. The correct interpretation should be that the elements from the specified index to the old size of the list are shifted to the right by one position. Here is the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i));</code>

This assert statement correctly captures the requirement that starting from the specified index, each element is shifted to the right by one position.
